From e13a8074358d26bed28ad08d2e48066677e61d92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritika Chopra <r.chopra@vyos.io>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 20:15:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] T9238: pppoe/disc: fix free_net memmove count and overlap
 handling (port from accel-ppp 315)

free_net() compacts the nets[] array by sliding entries left after
removing one:

    memcpy(nets + i, nets + i + 1, net_cnt - i - 1);

Two bugs:

  1. The count is a raw element count, not a byte count. nets[] holds
     'struct disc_net *' pointers, so only (net_cnt - i - 1) bytes are
     moved instead of (net_cnt - i - 1) * sizeof(nets[0]). On the usual
     8-byte-pointer build, 7 of every 8 surviving pointers are lost,
     leaving uninitialised holes in the array.

  2. Source and destination overlap (nets + i and nets + i + 1), so
     memcpy is undefined behaviour. The correct primitive is memmove.

Switch to memmove and multiply the count by sizeof(nets[0]).

Authored-by: khedor <khedor@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit a68821aecb2fecfc7c35fd5d49867f202d64df7f)
---
 accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c b/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c
index d844c7fd..17ebd4ec 100644
--- a/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c
+++ b/accel-pppd/ctrl/pppoe/disc.c
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ static void free_net(struct disc_net *net)
 	pthread_mutex_lock(&nets_lock);
 	for (i = 0; i < MAX_NET; i++) {
 		if (nets[i] == net) {
-			memcpy(nets + i, nets + i + 1, net_cnt - i - 1);
+			memmove(nets + i, nets + i + 1, (net_cnt - i - 1) * sizeof(nets[0]));
 			net_cnt--;
 			break;
 		}
